The '''2026 Norfolk County Council election''' took  place on 7 May 2026 to elect members to [[Norfolk County Council]] in [[Norfolk]], [[England]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=31 January 2023 |title=Election timetable in England |url=https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/election-timetable-in-england/election-timetable-in-england#district-councils2 |access-date=4 September 2024 |publisher=[[Electoral Commission (UK)|Electoral Commission]]}}</ref> All 84 seats were elected. This was on the same day as other [[2026 United Kingdom local elections|2026 local elections]].

==Background==
At the [[2021 Norfolk County Council election|2021 election]], the Conservatives won a majority of seats.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2021-05-07 |title=Elections 2021: Conservatives hold control of Norfolk |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-england-norfolk-57021786 |access-date=2024-11-29 |work=BBC News |language=en-GB}}</ref> The 2026 election was held under new electoral division boundaries.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2021-05-11 |title=Mapped: How will the electoral changes impact you? |url=https://www.edp24.co.uk/news/20653304.mapped-will-electoral-changes-impact/ |access-date=2024-11-29 |website=Eastern Daily Press |language=en}}</ref>
Having delayed the elections from 2025 to 2026, the government announced plans to further delay them until 2027, but abandoned this following a legal challenge by [[Reform UK]].<ref name="bbc16feb26">{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c70ne31d884o|date=16 February 2026|title=Government abandons plans to delay 30 council elections|website=BBC News}}</ref>

According to a BBC report in March 2026 citing Conservative sources, the party's own internal polling was showing it facing the loss of most of its seats on the county council in May.<ref>{{cite news |title=Badenoch insists party has 'best offer' for county |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cx2rnd58q70o |agency=BBC News}}</ref>

