==Results==
Reform won the most seats at 40, doing particullarly well in [[South Norfolk]], a former Tory stronghold.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Thompson |first1=Emily-Rose |title=Norfolk local elections 2026: Broadland and South Norfolk results |url=https://www.eveningnews24.co.uk/news/26089958.norfolk-local-elections-2026-broadland-south-norfolk-results/ |website=[[Norwich Evening News]] |access-date=8 May 2026}}</ref> This left them just three seats shy of a majority in the county council, partly due to the success of [[Great Yarmouth First]] (connected with Restore Britain) and the Liberal Democrats. In [[North Norfolk]] there were ten council seats up for election, with the Liberal Democrats winning seven of them, while Great Yarmouth First won all nine seats in the [[Borough of Great Yarmouth]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Ozanne |first1=Phoebe |title=Norfolk local elections 2026: Lib Dems' north Norfolk win |url=https://www.northnorfolknews.co.uk/news/26090593.norfolk-local-elections-2026-lib-dems-north-norfolk-win/ |website=[[North Norfolk News]] |access-date=8 May 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Robinson |first1=Ben |title=Norfolk local elections 2026: Clean sweep for Great Yarmouth First |url=https://www.edp24.co.uk/news/26091071.norfolk-local-elections-2026-clean-sweep-great-yarmouth-first/ |website=[[Norwich Evening News]] |access-date=8 May 2026}}</ref>

